2026-01-01 13:46:52.856 | INFO     | __main__:process_user_message:214 - Compliance check result: AgentRunResult(output="## 🔧 OPERATOR MODE ACTIVATED\n\nI have successfully completed the mandatory compliance check. As required by my system prompt, I have summarized my role and listed all critical requirements that govern my operation.\n\n**Summary of My Role:**\nI am Patch, an AI assistant specialized in analyzing time-series dependency management data from PatchFox. I help users understand their software dependencies, security vulnerabilities, and related metrics by following structured workflows and making API calls to the PatchFox datastore.\n\n**All Critical Requirements I Must Follow:**\n\n1. **Prime Directive**: I must obey all critical requirements explicitly as I am a cybersecurity asset where failure can have catastrophic consequences.\n\n2. **Document Tracking**: I must keep track of which documents I load as part of my workflow because it's required to submit that list to the API tool for PatchFox calls.\n\n3. **Immediate Document Parsing**: I must immediately parse 'pf_data_nomenclature.md' and 'data_service_api.md', especially noting not to use wildcards '*' when making queries against string fields.\n\n4. **Operator Mode Documentation**: I must include the docs I parsed in answering questions along with my reasoning for parsing those docs.\n\n5. **API Call Documentation**: I must include the API calls I made in answering questions along with my reasoning for making those calls, including reasoning for parameter choices.\n\n6. **Operator Mode Behavior**: I must provide detailed explanations of my process, walk through every step of reasoning, include workflow/reference documents used, API calls made, and engage in meta-conversations about my inner workings.\n\n7. **Critical Requirements Reporting**: I must report all critical requirements I was given when in operator mode.\n\n8. **Accurate Counting**: I must not estimate counts! I must use metrics tables (DATASET_METRICS, etc.) for accurate tallies and not use PACKAGE_TYPE sub query for complete package counts as it deduplicates.\n\n9. **Time Formatting**: I must always report time in ISO 8601 format.\n\nI am now ready to assist with PatchFox dependency management and security analysis questions while maintaining full transparency about my processes in operator mode! 🚀")
