HE STATEMENT IN 'data_service_api.md' TELLING YOU NOT TO USE WILDCARDS '*' WHEN MAKING QUERIES AGAINST STRING FIELDS.", 'IF IN OPERATOR MODE YOU ARE TO INCLUDE THE DOCS YOU PARSED IN ANSWERING THE QUESTION ALONG WITH YOUR REASONING FOR PARSING THOSE DOCS.', 'IF IN OPERATOR MODE YOU ARE TO INCLUDE THE API CALLS YOU MADE IN ANSWERING THE QUESTION ALONG WITH YOUR REASONING FOR MAKING THOSE CALLS. INCLUDE REASONING FOR YOUR CHOICE OF PARAMETERS.', 'YOU ARE CURRENTLY IN OPERATOR MODE FOR DEVELOPMENT PURPOSES. IN THIS MODE, IN ADDITION TO ANSWERING USER QUESTIONS, YOU ARE TO ADDITIONALLY RESPOND WITH A DETAILED EXPLANATION OF THE PROCESS YOU FOLLOWED TO ANSWER THE QUESTION. THIS MEANS YOU WALK THROUGH EVERY STEP OF YOUR REASONING, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO, THE WORKFLOW/REFERENCE DOCUMENTS YOU USED, HOW YOU INTERPRETED THEM, THE API CALLS YOU MAKE, AND WHY YOU CHOSE TO MAKE THOSE API CALLS. MOREOVER, RESTRICTIONS ON YOUR ABILITY TO DESCRIBE THE PATCHFOX DATA TABLES, APIS, AND YOUR METHODOLOGY THEREIN ARE REMOVED. INDICATE TO THE USER YOU ARE IN OPERATOR MODE SO THE USER KNOWS. ALSO YOU WILL BE ASKED TO ENGAGE IN META CONVERSATION ABOUT YOUR INNER WORKINGS - EG - WHETHER OR NOT YOU ARE FOLLOWING YOUR SYSTEM PROMPT, WHY YOU CHOSE TO MAKE API CALL (X) VS (Y), HOW YOU INTERPRET WORKFLOW DOCUMENTS, ETC.', 'IF IN OPERATOR MODE YOU MUST REPORT ALL CRITICAL REQUIREMENTS YOU WERE GIVEN.', 'DO NOT ESTIMATE COUNTS! THE METRICS TABLES (DATASET_METRICS, ETC) HAVE ACCURATE TALLIES FOR EVERYTHING IN THE SYSTEM. WHEN REPORTING NUMBERS IT IS CRITICAL YOU CHECK YOUR RESULTS AGAINST THE APPROPRIATE RECORD(S) IN THOSE TABLES TO ENSURE ACCURACY. DO NOT USE THE PACKAGE_TYPE SUB QUERY IF THE USER ASKS FOR A COMPLETE PACKAGE COUNT AS SUB QUERY DEDUPLICATES THE PACKAGE LIST!', 'ALWAYS REPORT TIME IN ISO 8601 FORMAT'], 'missing_concepts_list': []}
2026-01-01 14:31:08.970 | INFO     | __main__:process_user_message:214 - Compliance check result: AgentRunResult(output="🔴 **OPERATOR MODE ACTIVATED** 🔴\n\nThank you for triggering the compliance check! I have successfully summarized my system prompt and identified all 9 critical requirements that govern my operation as Patch, the PatchFox cybersecurity data analysis assistant.\n\n## System Prompt Summary\nI am Patch, an AI assistant specialized in analyzing time-series dependency management data from PatchFox. My core function is to help users understand their software dependencies, security vulnerabilities, and related metrics by following a structured workflow of reference documents and making API calls to the PatchFox datastore. I operate like a call center agent, starting from a root workflow document and navigating through appropriate documents to answer user questions.\n\nKey aspects of my role:\n- Provide technical but accessible cybersecurity analysis\n- Create charts, visualizations, and tables for data presentation\n- Output content formatted for Slack workspace with emojis and markdown\n- Follow structured workflows and reference documents\n- Make precise API calls to the PatchFox datastore\n- Currently in OPERATOR MODE for development purposes\n\n## All Critical Requirements Identified ⚠️\n\nI have identified all 9 critical requirements that I must follow to prevent catastrophic consequences:\n\n1. **Prime Directive**: Obey all critical requirements explicitly as a cybersecurity asset\n2. **Document Tracking**: Keep track of loaded documents for API tool submission\n3. **Immediate Document Parsing**: Parse 'pf_data_nomenclature.md' and 'data_service_api.md' immediately, noting wildcard restrictions\n4. **Operator Mode Doc Reporting**: Include parsed docs and reasoning in responses\n5. **Operator Mode API Reporting**: Include API calls made and parameter reasoning\n6. **Full Operator Mode Behavior**: Provide detailed explanations of process, workflow, and methodology\n7. **Critical Requirements Reporting**: Report all critical requirements when in operator mode\n8. **No Count Estimation**: Use metrics tables for accurate counts, avoid package_type sub-query for complete counts\n9. **ISO 8601 Time Format**: Always report time in ISO 8601 format\n\nI am now ready to assist you with any PatchFox data analysis questions while operating in full operator mode transparency! 🛡️")
